---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';

/**
 * Versão inglesa da Política de Privacidade.
 *
 * Tradução do documento português, que continua a ser a versão de referência
 * — é a que vale perante a CNPD, e qualquer alteração feita lá tem de ser
 * reflectida aqui. As referências ao RGPD mantêm a numeração dos artigos.
 *
 * TODO(cliente): a par do português, rever com apoio jurídico antes de
 * publicar e preencher os campos marcados como pendentes.
 */
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Homeostase Vita"
  description="How Homeostase Vita processes the personal data collected through this site, under the GDPR."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Who processes your data</h2>
  <p>
    The controller of the personal data collected on this site is
    <strong>{site.legalName}</strong>, with its address at {site.address.street},
    {site.address.postalCode}&nbsp;{site.address.locality}, Portugal.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any question about this policy or about your data, contact us by email at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or by telephone on
    {site.phone.display}.
  </p>
  <p>Tax number (NIF): 218520115</p>

  <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect only what is necessary in order to contact you:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Where</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Name, phone, email and reason for contact</td>
        <td>Booking form</td>
        <td>Responding to the request and scheduling the consultation</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Aggregated browsing data</td>
        <td>Measurement cookies</td>
        <td>Understanding how the site is used — only with your permission</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The "reason for contact" field is free text. We ask that you do not include detailed
    clinical information there — that conversation belongs in the consultation, not in a
    form.
  </p>

  <h2>3. On what legal basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Consent</strong> (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR) — for the booking form and for
      measurement cookies. You may withdraw it at any time, without affecting the
      lawfulness of processing carried out beforehand.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Pre-contractual steps</strong> (Article 6(1)(b)) — where the contact is
      intended to book a consultation.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. For how long</h2>
  <p>
    Contact requests that do not result in a consultation are deleted after 12 months.
    If you become our patient, the data is then retained under the legal obligations
    applicable to clinical records.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Who has access</h2>
  <p>
    The data is accessed only by those at Homeostase Vita who need it in order to
    respond to your request. We use technical service providers — site hosting and the
    form delivery service — who process the data on our behalf and are bound by
    confidentiality.
  </p>
  <p>We do not sell or pass on your data to third parties for commercial purposes.</p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask us at any time for access to, rectification, erasure, restriction or
    portability of your data, as well as object to the processing. Simply write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you consider that your data is not being processed correctly, you may lodge a
    complaint with the Portuguese Data Protection Authority (CNPD) —
    <a href="https://www.cnpd.pt" rel="noopener">www.cnpd.pt</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over an encrypted connection (HTTPS) and the form data is
    transmitted by POST, never in the page address. The typefaces are hosted on this
    domain, so reading the site does not generate requests to third-party servers.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated. The date of the last revision is shown at the top of the
    page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
